vertrice: changes relative to voidrice

Upstream base: voidrice commit b45fc56 ("profile remove GTK2_RC_FILES").
Everything below came after it. OPENBSD.md gives the reasons in full;
`git log b45fc56..` gives each commit.


Processes and signals

- setsid(1) is not in OpenBSD. New `detach` (nohup, background, output
  to /dev/null) replaces every `setsid -f`.
- pidof and killall become pgrep and pkill; script lookups use pgrep -f.
- OpenBSD has no real-time signals, so dwmblocks cannot build. New
  `sbar` (ksh) runs the status blocks and redraws on SIGUSR1; new
  `sb-refresh` sends that signal after checking the pid is sbar's.
  Clickable blocks do nothing for now (they needed sigqueue(3)).

Shell

- ksh replaces zsh: `~/.profile` sets ENV to `.config/ksh/kshrc`.
  What zsh did that ksh cannot is listed at the end of the kshrc.
- Aliases use only flags OpenBSD's tools have. sudo becomes doas; the
  rsync alias uses openrsync from base.
- `config`: git on the bare dotfiles repository, with $HOME as work tree.

X session and window manager

- cwm and xterm from base are the default; dwm and st are opt-ins
  (WM and TERMINAL in the profile).
- `.config/cwm/cwmrc` carries voidrice's dwm keys to cwm. New `keys`
  (Super+F1) lists them in dmenu; new `scratch` gives the scratchpads;
  `sb-show` (Super+b) shows the status line as a notification.
- xinitrc also serves xenodm (`~/.xsession`), starts the D-Bus session
  bus first, and starts ssh-agent only when none runs.
- Idle lock with xidle and xlock from base. slock is gone. The system
  stage installs `/etc/apm/suspend` and `/etc/apm/hibernate`, which send
  xidle SIGUSR1 so X is locked before the machine sleeps.
- `nightlight` (Super+F4) warms the screen with sct.

Sound

- sndiod replaces PipeWire and PulseAudio; volume through sndioctl;
  mpd outputs to sndio; dmenurecord records from sndio.

Status blocks

- Every block reads OpenBSD's own sources: apm, wsconsctl, sysctl
  hw.sensors and kern.cp_time2, ifconfig, netstat -ibn, top, df.
- sb-cpu shows temperature and CPU speed.
- Network blocks lock with mkdir in /tmp instead of flock(1) in
  XDG_RUNTIME_DIR (OpenBSD has neither); state files moved to ~/.cache.
- Removed: sb-pacpackages, sb-popupgrade (pacman).

GNU syntax

- sed, grep, stat, file, date, shuf, numfmt, shred and mktemp calls use
  BSD and POSIX forms. getbib's formatter is one awk pass.

Base tools in place of packages

- Every curl (and rssget's wget) call uses base ftp(1). pauseallmpv
  uses base nc(1) -NU in place of socat. rssget and sb-ticker are POSIX
  sh, not bash.
- setbg without xwallpaper sets the root window to the theme's
  background colour (xsetroot); lf's scope without bat shows the start
  of a text file (head).

Packages in place of ones with no port

- qndl queues with nq instead of task-spooler; sb-tasks counts its jobs.
- torwrap and sb-torrent open tremc instead of stig.

Palette

- theme also colours dunst and zathura, and the root window without
  xwallpaper. pywal is opt-in (PALETTE=wal); its postrun is sh.

WiFi

- New `dmenuwifi` (sb-internet's click, in place of nmtui): pick a
  network in dmenu, join it with ifconfig, optionally add it to
  /etc/hostname.IF.

Browser

- larbs.js's Firefox tweaks moved to qutebrowser's config.py; the
  .config/sxiv link is gone.

Files and drives

- New `ext` extracts every archive type by name; lf's E key calls it.
- mounter and unmounter rewritten on voidrice's flow: partitions from
  disklabel, softraid CRYPTO through bioctl in place of LUKS, Android
  through simple-mtpfs, fstab entries by DUID, every mount nosuid,nodev,
  the system disk never offered.
- USB notices: `hotplug-attach` (run by hotplugd as root) and
  `hotplug-watch` (in the session, with entr). Nothing mounts by itself.
- Removed: dmenumountcifs, dmenupass, remapd, cron/checkup.

Editors

- nvim is the daily editor; vi (nvi, base) is the fallback with its own
  `.config/vi/exrc`. Root always gets vi. nvim's :w!! is removed.

Root and doas

- `doas.conf` (one rule for wheel, no nopass) and `root.kshrc` for root.

Browsers

- qutebrowser is $BROWSER; chromium on Super+Shift+w.

Look

- Day and night palettes (`theme`, switched by the clock or Super+F8),
  IBM Plex fonts, cwm frames after OpenBSD's fvwm, dunst to match.

ThinkPad X220

- Touchpad off for good (mouse.tp.disable=1 in /etc/wsconsctl.conf,
  from the system stage), TrackPoint wheel scrolling in `remaps`, notes
  on Fn keys, backlight, lid, battery and console.
- Webcam: `vertrice-install -v` sets kern.video.record=1 and adds
  /dev/video0 to /etc/fbtab (a call needs -r too); Super+F11 is base
  video(1), as voidrice's F11 was the webcam.

Install and tests

- `vertrice-install`: a home stage (the dotfiles) and a system stage
  (packages, doas, root's shell, hotplugd, login class for browsers,
  apmd, obsdfreqd, unwind, Caps Lock as Escape on the console, battery
  charge limit). Prints its plan without -y; running it again changes
  nothing. -e also installs pkglist.extra.
- Package lists: `pkglist` (core) and `pkglist.extra` (features you
  can skip), each package argued in OPENBSD.md.
- `.local/share/openbsd/check` tests on the machine what could not be
  tested off it.
- `.local/share/vertrice/tests/run`: regression suite against mocked
  OpenBSD commands.

Fixes found by the tests

- shortcuts no longer runs rm -f on /dev/null (as root it deleted it).
- mounter no longer offers unmounted partitions of the system disk.

Not ported

- `sd` (needs a helper for KERN_PROC_CWD). See OPENBSD.md, "Not ported,
  or not tested".
